    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "story",
        "type": "story",
        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "The square garden"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "A square garden has side (a + b). What is its area? Splitting it into four rectangles shows (a + b) squared = a squared + 2ab + b squared - and this is an identity."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "identity",
          "square identities",
          "difference of squares",
          "(x + a)(x + b)",
          "trinomial square",
          "sum and difference of cubes",
          "factorise steps"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "An identity is true for every value of the variables.\n(a + b) squared = a squared + 2ab + b squared and (a - b) squared = a squared - 2ab + b squared.\na squared - b squared = (a + b)(a - b).\n(x + a)(x + b) = x squared + (a + b)x + ab.\n(a + b + c) squared = a squared + b squared + c squared + 2ab + 2bc + 2ca.\na cubed + b cubed = (a + b)(a squared - ab + b squared) and a cubed - b cubed = (a - b)(a squared + ab + b squared).\nTo factorise, look first for a common factor, then try an identity, then split the middle term."
        }
      },
